<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  REFERENCE COPY. The supported way to install this is:

      codeconnect daemon install

  which generates the same document with the paths resolved on *this* machine —
  the ccd binary, and a PATH built from where tmux, git, tailscale and claude
  actually are. A template can only encode one guess at those, and launchd's
  diagnostic for a wrong one is a job that never runs.

      codeconnect daemon status      plist, launchd job and live daemon
      codeconnect daemon restart     launchctl kickstart -k
      codeconnect daemon uninstall   bootout and remove the plist

  If you would rather install by hand, substitute __HOME__ and bootstrap it:

      sed "s|__HOME__|$HOME|g" mac/launchd/com.codeconnect.ccd.plist \
        > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.codeconnect.ccd.plist
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.codeconnect.ccd.plist

  Notes that are not obvious and cost real debugging time:

  * LaunchAgent, not LaunchDaemon: ccd needs the user's login session for the
    keychain (APNs .p8) and for the tailnet identity.
  * launchd starts a process with a minimal environment and *no shell PATH*, so
    PATH is set explicitly here and every external binary (tmux, tailscale,
    git, claude) is additionally resolved from an absolute candidate list in
    code. Both, because the two failures look identical from the outside.
  * KeepAlive/SuccessfulExit=false restarts ccd if it crashes but respects a
    clean exit, so `launchctl bootout` does not fight a restart loop.
  * ThrottleInterval is launchd's floor between restarts. Five seconds stops a
    crash-looping job from spinning a core; it is also why a `kill -9` can take
    up to five seconds to recover rather than milliseconds.
  * The log files below are truncated in place by ccd itself once they pass
    `log_max_bytes`. launchd holds them open, so rotating by rename would leave
    it appending to an unlinked inode — the log would stop growing and the disk
    would keep filling, with nothing to see.
  * ccd is deliberately NOT the parent of any agent. Sessions live in the
    `tmux -L codeconnect` server; restarting this agent costs a reconnect.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.codeconnect.ccd</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__HOME__/.codeconnect/bin/ccd</string>
    </array>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <dict>
        <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
        <false/>
    </dict>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>5</integer>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>__HOME__/.codeconnect/bin:__HOME__/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>__HOME__</string>
        <key>CODECONNECT_LOG</key>
        <string>info</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.codeconnect/logs/ccd.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.codeconnect/logs/ccd.err.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Interactive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
